# CSS and Styling Conventions

## CSS Modules

- Use CSS Modules for component-specific styles (`style.module.css`)
- Follow BEM-like naming: `taskList`, `taskListEmpty`, `taskListEmptyContent`
- Import styles: `import styles from "./style.module.css"`

## Design System Variables

Global CSS custom properties defined in [src/styles/variables.css](mdc:src/styles/variables.css):

```css
/* Use semantic color tokens */
color: var(--text-base);
background-color: var(--container);
border-color: var(--accent-primary);

/* Typography */
font-family: var(--font-body);
font-family: var(--font-heading); /* for headers */
```

## Component Patterns

```css
/* Use CSS custom properties for component variants */
.btn {
  --__bg: var(--bg, transparent);
  --__font-size: var(--font-size, 1rem);
  --__padding: var(--padding, 0.5rem 1rem);
}

/* Nested selectors for card structure */
.card {
  .card__header {
  }
  .card__body {
  }
  .card__footer {
  }
}
```

## Layout Conventions

- Use flexbox for layouts with gap property
- Implement proper scrolling with `scrollbar-width: thin`
- Use `min-height` and `max-height` for constrained containers
- Responsive design with CSS custom properties for sizing

## Button Styling

```css
.addTaskBtn {
  --font-size: 0.9rem;
  --icon-size: 1rem;
  --padding: 0.3rem 0.6rem;
}
```

## Animation Patterns

```css
.underlineAnimation {
  &::after {
    content: "";
    transition: all 0.3s ease;
  }

  &:hover::after {
    width: 100%;
  }
}
```

## Empty States

- Use meaningful icons and messages for empty states
- Center content with flexbox
- Provide clear call-to-action guidance
